{
  "name": "letspepper-reels-worker",
  "main": "src/index.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-01-01",
  // ARMED 2026-08-11 for cutting-board-announce. Only its `announce` item is
  // status "pending"; the other four are "draft" and post nothing until an
  // operator flips them, because nino.chavez.photo's publish path has never been
  // exercised and the campaign's rule is to confirm `announce` lands first.
  // announce carries scheduledAt 2026-08-12T01:00Z, so it fires at that tick and
  // is NOT gated by ALLOWED_HOURS_UTC. See
  // creative/campaigns/cutting-board-announce.md.
  //
  // poblano-2026-cancellation stays listed and stays inert. DISARMED 2026-07-28 —
  // the Poblano Open was cancelled (not enough teams), so the finale campaign is
  // over. Every poblano-2026-finale item had already published by then
  // (details-day, the last one, went out 2026-07-28T17:00Z to Instagram and the
  // Facebook Page), so nothing was cut off mid-drip. Its single item was flipped
  // and published on 2026-07-29T00:52:26Z (media 18358416091211728), so the queue
  // is spent, not pending — verified in KV 2026-08-12. This comment previously
  // said "draft", which was true when written and stopped being true that day.
  // See scripts/social-publish/queue/poblano-2026-cancellation.json.
  //
  // Hourly cron: each run finishes any in-flight container, then posts at most
  // ONE due item. Items carrying scheduledAt fire at their planned time
  // (scheduledAt gates them, NOT ALLOWED_HOURS_UTC). This worker replaced the
  // local launchd drip (com.letspepper.reels, disabled at cutover) as the sole poster.
  "triggers": { "crons": ["0 * * * *"] },
  "kv_namespaces": [
    { "binding": "QUEUE", "id": "c2e5f3feb71f4804b801eb8b56782442" }
  ],
  "vars": {
    // event slugs in PRIORITY order — newest/highest-priority FIRST. Each slot
    // posts from the first event with a DUE item; older events backfill only when
    // newer ones are exhausted. poblano-2026-finale is deliberately NOT listed
    // any more: it is fully published, and re-arming it could only re-post promo
    // for a cancelled event. jpo-teams / flickday-grass-drip / bell-pepper-2026
    // sit inert in KV — re-add to ACTIVE_EVENTS to resume.
    // Listing an event is not enough to publish from it: its KV queue must also
    // carry meta.route, seeded by seed-kv.mjs from graph-routes.json. Neither
    // queue listed here has one (read 2026-09-21), and neither has a pending item.
    //
    // gallery-announce (added 2026-09-25, source change only — this Worker has NOT
    // been deployed with it): Nino's standing "gallery announcements" route
    // (see graph-routes.json). Every item carries scheduledAt — since 2026-09-26,
    // the first slot in THIS var (ALLOWED_HOURS_UTC) at or after the item's holdUntil,
    // not holdUntil itself (a fix: it used to equal holdUntil, so a hold clearing at
    // 2am would publish at 2am; the HELD phone alert now promises a specific slot, so
    // the code has to actually honor it — see notify.mjs's nextAllowedSlot and
    // build-gallery-announce.mjs's own comment). scheduledAt is still the ONLY gate —
    // any hour, never ALLOWED_HOURS_UTC directly — this listing is safe the moment
    // items exist because their scheduledAt is already computed FROM this var at
    // build time. Changing ALLOWED_HOURS_UTC does not retroactively move an already-
    // built item's scheduledAt — it only affects the NEXT album's build.
    // seed-kv.mjs --event gallery-announce --append --put has not been run, so
    // this Worker's KV holds no "gallery-announce" key at all. loadQueue() returns
    // null for a missing key and both postDuePending/resumeIfBuilding just skip it.
    "ACTIVE_EVENTS": "gallery-announce,cutting-board-announce,poblano-2026-cancellation",
    // UTC posting slots — the daily cap for LEGACY (no-scheduledAt) items only.
    // The cancellation item carries no scheduledAt, so it IS gated by these hours
    // once an operator flips it to pending: 17 = noon CDT, 22 = 5p CDT.
    "ALLOWED_HOURS_UTC": "17,22",
    // --- engagement sweep (see SWEEP.md) ---
    "SWEEP_ENABLED": "0",          // OFF for the finale migration — posting only; flip to "1" to re-enable the comment sweep
    "SWEEP_LOOKBACK_DAYS": "14",   // only sweep media newer than this
    "SWEEP_AUTOREPLY": "off",      // off | intent — DEFAULTS OFF (shadow-logs only)
    // No event is open for registration — the sweep's signup auto-reply must not
    // point at the cancelled finale's page. Homepage until the next season opens.
    "REGISTRATION_URL": "https://letspepper.com",
    // gallery-announce carousel budget (2026-09-26): external (Graph + ntfy) subrequests
    // one invocation may spend before deferring the rest to the next tick — see src/index.js's
    // makeBudget. Conservative default under the Workers Free plan's 50/invocation cap; this
    // account's own cron-trigger count (19+ across existing Workers, Free caps at 5/account)
    // is evidence it's on Paid, which defaults to 10,000/invocation — raise this once that's
    // confirmed from the dashboard rather than inferred. See SETUP.md "Cloudflare plan".
    "SUBREQUEST_BUDGET": "40"
  },
  "observability": { "enabled": true }
  // secrets (set via `wrangler secret put`): IG_ACCESS_TOKEN, FB_ACCESS_TOKEN,
  // TRIGGER_KEY. Meta exposes Instagram content and Facebook Page management
  // as separate app use cases, so keep their System User tokens isolated.
  // Optional dedicated Page-token overrides:
  // FB_LETSPEPPER_ACCESS_TOKEN, FB_FLICKDAY_ACCESS_TOKEN,
  // FB_NINOPHOTO_ACCESS_TOKEN.
  // NTFY_TOPIC (added for gallery-announce phone notifications, 2026-09-26): the ntfy.sh
  // topic from 1Password (`ntfy gallery-announce`). Absent means the Worker silently skips
  // notifying — never a publish failure. See notify.mjs and SETUP.md "Arming gallery-announce".
  // REVIEW_KEY (added for the /review page, 2026-09-26): view + cancel auth for GET /review
  // and POST /review/cancel — a SEPARATE secret from TRIGGER_KEY, which /review can never
  // reach (it has no access to /run). From 1Password (`Cloudflare letspepper-reels-worker
  // review-key`). Absent means every /review* request 403s — never "any key matches". See
  // SETUP.md "/review" and "Arming gallery-announce".
}
